Subject: Using tagAppendAttributes() more than once on the same tag
Message-ID: <IdgjZ8MmUPE.jZlRrKJa_YoJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/IdgjZ8MmUPE/m/jZlRrKJa_YoJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I noticed that tag attributes are stored as a named list in the `attribs` value of a shiny.tag

I wanted to add a class to a tag that already had a class, like so:

shiny::tagAppendAttributes(shiny::div("hello", class = "foo"), class = "bar")

This does work right and give me the desired output

<div class="foo bar">hello</div>

However, when I inspect the tag I see that the two classes are stored as two separate items

List of 3
 $ name : chr "div"
 $ attribs :List of 2
 ..$ class: chr "foo"
 ..$ class: chr "bar"
 $ children:List of 1
 ..$ : chr "hello"
 - attr(*, "class")= chr "shiny.tag"

This feels wrong, though it's probably not technically wrong? I was hoping the class would be a string "foo bar" but instead it just added "bar" as another class.  It does make it a bit more difficult to test for a specific class.

I'm just wondering if there is a more correct way to do what I'm doing (adding multiple values of the same attribute but not all at once) and if this behaviour is correct or undesired.

Thanks ShinyRs!

