Do you mean, if you're calling this app from the R console, how you would get the value back? The answer in that case would be using stopApp <http://shiny.rstudio.com/reference/shiny/latest/stopApp.html>().

Do you mean, how would you cause other things in the Shiny process to update according to that input? You would use reactive expressions, outputs, and observers--see chapters 4 and 6 in the Shiny tutorial <http://shiny.rstudio.com/tutorial/> and the section on "Reactive programming" in the Articles <http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/> area.

If you mean something else, it'd be helpful if you provided a little more context (e.g. what do you want to do with that variable?).

