Hello Joe,

Thanks again for the hints. I managed to get a nearly working app with two issues: (1) when I change the number of sliders, I get an error (it certainly has to do with proper cleaning of variables, no great deal); (2) the sliders "wobble" when I'm moving one of them.

Point (2) is the one I have no idea how to fix. Whenever I move a slider (say, slider 1), the values of the other ones (say, #2 and 3) are updated, as they should. But -- in my understanding-- this triggers the event linked to sl2 and sl3. Therefore, slider 2 updates sl1 and sl3. which in turn triggers 1 and 3 ... etc., and the net result is that the sliders oscillate before reaching a stable point. Surely the solution is about isolating one of the controls, but right now I cannot find out what I should isolate() and where!

Thanks !

Here is the code...

---- ui.R-----------

shinyUI(fluidPage(

  # Application title
  titlePanel("Demo app"),

  # Three sliders for values a, b and c -- total must be 100%
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
    numericInput("num", label = "Number of sliders", value = 3),
    uiOutput("sliders")
    ),
    # Write the result
    mainPanel(
      textOutput("result")
    )
  )
))

--- server.R------------

shinyServer(function(session, input, output) {

# Define the names of the variables used to describe the sliders
slidernames<-reactive({
# Placeholder
as.character(seq(1,input$num,by=1))
})

# Read the slider values
slidervals<-reactive({
m.prop<-lapply(slidernames(), function(m) {
                    return(input[[paste("sl",m,sep="")]])
                })
    m.prop<-unlist(m.prop)
    names(m.prop)<-slidernames()
    return(m.prop)
})

# The real meat of the code -- render the slider and create the binding

output$sliders <- renderUI({
  lapply(slidernames(), function(slidername) {

  ## Generate observeEvent
   observeEvent(input[[paste("sl",slidername,sep="")]], {
    # Identify the slider that will remain fixed (the one we just moved)
    fx<-slidername
    nf<-setdiff(slidernames(),slidername)

    # Read the values and normalize
    sv<-slidervals()
    ee<-sv[nf]
    ee_n<-ee/sum(ee)*(100-sv[fx])
    ee_n<-c(sv[fx],ee_n)
    names(ee_n)[1]<-fx

    # Move the non-fixed sliders
    lapply(nf, function(mm) {
                     updateSliderInput(session,paste("sl",mm,sep=""),
                     value=as.numeric(ee_n[mm]))
                 })
   cat("Slider",slidername,"\n")
   }) # End of observeEvent

   sliderInput(paste("sl",slidername,sep=""), slidername, min = 0, max = 100, value = 100/input$num)

  }) # End of lapply
}) # End of renderUI

output$result<- renderText({
slidervals()
})

})

