Normally the answer is to put the offending call (stockstxtclosure()) in a proper reactive context, but in this case I'd take the code of stockstxtclosure out of a reactive expression and just call it directly. You'll get the same error then when you call clientData$url_search; change it to isolate(clientData$url_search) and you should be good to go.

