I ended up by creating my own version of a pseudo file browser, which works interactively where R responds with the content from list.files()
(directories are listed with a + sign in front, and files are listed as simple files)

It's a rather complex combination of R, shiny, jQuery, Raphael and heavily customized Javascript code to combine everything... but it works.

Not sure if it is supported, but I am attaching a video capture as a demo.

Best,
Adrian

